flowchart BT
subgraph intro [Tutorial]
%% Major idea: Intro section to teach the player about activation, capacity upgrades, and the sword ability

    start["start"]
    %% Contents: Player spawns with 1 capacity and 1 HP.
    %% Golden path: player sees there is a door, but it is closed. Player experiments with UI until they manage to activate the key_store node
    %% Player learns: "Activation of a node = unlocking the door"
    key_store["Key Storage"]
    %% Ability: +4 HP
    %% Contents: 1 capacity upgrade. 4 health pickups. Switch_1: removes Wall_1. Door towards sword_room blocked by Wall_1.
    %% Golden path: Player picks up the capacity upgrade, allowing them to activate sword_room. Player can then hit the switch to go into sword_room.
    %% Player learns: "Activation of a node = gaining an ability"
    %% Player learns: "The sword ability can be used to hit switches"
    start --- key_store
end
key_store --- sword_room
sword_room --- boots_room

subgraph sword-branch [Sword]
%% Major idea: Player learns combat basics. Tree allows player to choose a Spear mod, a Heavy mod, or Neither. Strength increase works in conjunction with any choice. Clearing weapons_landing is necessary for reaching miniboss.

    sword_room["Sword"]
    %% Ability: Sword
    %% Contents: 2-3 bats.
    %% Clear condition: defeat all enemies
    %% On clear: capacity upgrade appears
    %% Golden path: Player defeats the enemies and sees that an upgrade appears. The player must make their first choice and explore the rest of the dungeon.
    %% Player learns: "Defeating all enemies can make collectibles appear"
    %% Player learns: "Not all paths can remain open at once"
    %% Room goal: teach the unmodified attack in a readable first engagement; current encounter is a functional placeholder.
    weapons_1["Spear Mod"]
    %% Ability: modifications that make the sword significantly narrower and longer range.
    %% Room idea: a threat approaching along an open lane rewards reach; a second threat from another angle exposes narrow coverage. Keep the first lesson readable.
    %% Candidate reward: 1 capacity revealed on clear, to fund weapons_landing. Clear condition and encounter tuning remain TBD.
    weapons_2["Heavy Mod"]
    %% Ability: modifications that make the sword moderately wider and longer range, moderately more powerful, and significantly slower. Player rooted from attack through sword cooldown; Dash can move the player without ending the restriction or cooldown.
    %% Room idea: a high-HP enemy demonstrates damage; a readable second threat or approach makes the choice of recovery position matter. Avoid overwhelming the first lesson.
    %% Candidate reward: 1 capacity revealed on clear, to fund weapons_landing. Clear condition and encounter tuning remain TBD.
    weapons_landing["Health Mod"]
    %% Ability: +5 HP increase
    %% Room idea: a modest mixed encounter fair with Spear, Heavy, or neither, making this a shared proving room. A separate health pickup could let the player use the increased maximum HP; allocation itself does not heal.
    %% Clear condition: TBD, but should be meaningful because this node is a proposed miniboss requirement. Reward: Gold placeholder pending overall funding.
    weapons_bonus["Strength Up"]
    %% Ability: moderate attack power increase
    %% Room idea: a durable enemy and geometry that still rewards movement demonstrate increased damage without necessarily adding Heavy's rooted restriction. Clear condition TBD; reward Gold placeholder pending overall funding.
end
sword_room --- weapons_1 --- weapons_landing
sword_room --- weapons_2 --- weapons_landing
weapons_1 x-.-x weapons_2 %% mutually exclusive nodes
sword_room --- weapons_landing
weapons_landing --- weapons_bonus
%% Budget hypothesis: after the Sword reward, one available capacity funds Spear, Heavy, or the direct landing. A modifier-room capacity reward could fund the landing.
%% Open question: if Spear and Heavy each contain a permanent reward, a player can eventually refund/reallocate and collect both. Decide whether to encourage that exploration or design a shared reward.

subgraph boots-branch [Boots]
%% Major idea: Player learns movement/exploration basics. Player must choose boots_1 or boots_2 before clearing boots_room. Clearing boots_room is necessary for reaching miniboss.
%% Funding hypothesis: Player enters boots_room with 0 unspent capacity. Assume boots_1, boots_2, and boots_landing each cost 1; validate these costs and the full allocation/refund route.

    boots_room["Boots"]
    %% Ability: Dash
    %% Contents: Open area for safely trying Dash, with access to boots_1, boots_2, and miniboss doors. wall_1 initially blocks access to boots_landing door and switch_1. Make the blocked route visible. switch_1 opens wall_1. Tokens scattered through the room, with at least one behind wall_1. One capacity upgrade is accessible before the room is cleared, potentially in a chest or side area.
    %% Clear condition: collect all tokens
    %% Clear reward: Gold placeholder; revisit as capacity after the overall budget is traced.
    %% Golden path: player initially sees the switch and cannot access it. The first capacity upgrade funds either boots_1 or boots_2. Quick Step takes the route through boots_landing and re-enters from that door; Phase Dash may instead cross a narrow wall as an alternate solution.
    %% Tokens reset on departure while uncleared, so make the final collection route clear and avoid punishing early exploration. Check switch toggling and safe exits.
    boots_1["Phase Dash"]
    %% Ability: Phase Dash (dash can go through obstacles and enemies without taking damage). Player rooted during dash cooldown.
    %% Contents: a narrow obstacle with a safe landing demonstrates phasing; a thicker obstacle or invalid destination can communicate its limit, with a walkable alternative. A later encounter may explore landing position and rooted recovery once contact and timing rules are settled. Clear condition: TBD. On clear: reveal 1 capacity upgrade to fund boots_landing.
    %% Phase Dash may cross the boots_room wall, so clearing boots_room need not require visiting boots_landing.
    boots_2["Quick Step"]
    %% Ability: modifications that make the dash go farther and have a shorter cooldown
    %% Contents: open lanes or a central obstacle and enemies encourage repeated repositioning, making dash distance and shorter cooldown apparent without requiring phasing. Clear condition: TBD. On clear: reveal 1 capacity upgrade to fund boots_landing.
    boots_landing["Health Mod"]
    %% Ability: +5 HP increase
    %% Contents: make the door to the far side of boots_room's wall easy to find, so returning and opening the shortcut is legible. A modest challenge should work for either dash option. Separate healing could complement the max-HP upgrade. Clear condition: TBD. Reward: Gold placeholder; revisit after budgeting.
    boots_bonus["Speed Up"]
    %% Ability: moderate movement speed increase
    %% Contents: an obstacle or encounter where ordinary movement and positioning between dashes help, regardless of which dash option is active. Clear condition: TBD. Reward: Gold placeholder; revisit after budgeting.
    boots_flippers["Flippers"]
    %% Ability: flippers
    %% Contents: visible water and a worthwhile destination beyond it. Wide water could demonstrate the difference between Flippers and Phase Dash's limited crossing range. Clear condition: TBD. Reward: Gold placeholder; revisit after budgeting.
    boots_room --- boots_1 --- boots_landing
    boots_room --- boots_2 --- boots_landing
    boots_1 x-.-x boots_2 %% mutually exclusive nodes
    %% The two route rewards are separate and both may eventually be collected by refunding and revisiting the other route. Include both in the global budget.

    boots_room --- boots_landing    
    boots_landing --- boots_bonus
    boots_landing --- boots_flippers
end
weapons_landing --> miniboss %% prerequisite. weapons_landing must be both cleared and active.
boots_room --> miniboss %% prerequisite. boots_room must be both cleared and active.
miniboss
